    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider the function \(y=\cos x\) for \(0\le x\le 2\pi\).</p>

<p>The graph of the function is shown below.</p>

[[jsxgraph]]
    var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
        boundingbox: [-0.5, 1.5, 2*Math.PI + 0.5, -1.5],
        axis: true,
        showCopyright: false,
        showNavigation: false,
        grid: true
    });

    var f = function(x) {
        return Math.cos(x);
    };

    board.create('functiongraph', [f, 0, 2*Math.PI], {
        strokeColor: '#1565C0',
        strokeWidth: 3
    });
[[/jsxgraph]]

<p><strong>(a)</strong> Use the graph to determine the value of \(y\) at each given value of \(x\).</p>

<p>1. When \(x=0\), \(y=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>

<p>2. When \(x=\frac{\pi}{2}\), \(y=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>

<p>3. When \(x=\pi\), \(y=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>

<p>4. When \(x=\frac{3\pi}{2}\), \(y=\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]]</p>

<p>5. When \(x=2\pi\), \(y=\) [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]]</p>

<p><strong>(b)</strong> State the maximum and minimum values of the function on the given interval.</p>

<p>Maximum value: [[input:ans6]] [[validation:ans6]]</p>

<p>Minimum value: [[input:ans7]] [[validation:ans7]]</p>]]></text>
